comments.body:
I think the fix here is to change the definition of `dt.offset_by` to always be monotonic.

That is, if `x <= y` then `x.dt.offset_by(c) <= y.dt.offset_by(c)` should always hold for any `c` (ignoring for a moment any overflows at the edges of the domains, which ideally error anyway).

@MarcoGorelli probably has some thoughts about this, but this is such a fundamental property of a function that's supposed to 'offset' that violating it feels very wrong. I understand an exact offset might not always be possible, but breaking monotonicity seems very hard to excuse.
